# Day 13

**32km / 9 hours**

Had intended to take the standard route and kayak across to Waikare and then walk for around 20km to get to the accommodation. However the weather was sufficiently poor as to cancel the kayaking so I ended up walking along some nice beaches from Paihia to Opua and taking the ferry across and walking from there. This meant I could leave earlier but the day would be around 30km, mostly on the road. 

![The water from the view of the ferry](./ferry-view.jpg)

It ended up being a fairly dull walking day after the ferry, punctuated by some heavy showers along the way. The main concern is about cars using the roads and trying to get out of their way and hoping for the best.

![One of many road signs along the way helpfully reminding drivers not to run me over](./road-sign.jpg)

 